{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_h6ngmoaqn7p4uhfskkqpktr2i23fcktl2zrpnrejhpdtcwlttp5a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found it: `pipe()`/`openpty()` fds aren't `CLOEXEC`, so the child inherits the pipe's **read** end — the pipe can never break, and the child blocks forever writing 2 MB. Let me fix:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":122714,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":122714,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55ad7133-91d4-4758-8739-8a336070d8f2","uuid":"25b178e4-b948-4848-94ae-9a7d12f9a8e9","timestamp":"2026-08-17T22:04:22.394Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_h6ngmoaqn7p4uhfskkqpktr2i23fcktl2zrpnrejhpdtcwlttp5a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01KBrnMwJPE5EsKh79Y3ACML","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np='tests/common/mod.rs'\ns=open(p).read()\n\n# 1) helper\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"/// Create a pipe; returns (read end, write end).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"/// Mark `fd` close-on-exec.\n///\n/// Critical for the pipe/pty helpers: `pipe(2)` and `openpty(3)` hand back\n/// *inheritable* descriptors, so without this the spawned child keeps a copy of\n/// the pipe's **read** end. The pipe could then never break (the child is its\n/// own reader), `SIGPIPE` would never be raised, and the child would block\n/// forever once the pipe filled up. `dup2` clears FD_CLOEXEC on the descriptor\n/// it creates, so the child still gets a working fd 0/1.\npub fn set_cloexec(fd: i32) {\n    unsafe {\n        let f = libc::fcntl(fd, libc::F_GETFD);\n        assert!(f >= 0, \"F_GETFD\");\n        assert!(libc::fcntl(fd, libc::F_SETFD, f | libc::FD_CLOEXEC) >= 0, \"F_SETFD\");\n    }\n}\n\n/// Create a pipe; returns (read end, write end).\"\"\")\n\n# 2) pipe_pair -> pipe2 O_CLOEXEC\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"pub fn pipe_pair() -> (i32, i32) {\n    let mut fds = [0i32; 2];\n    assert_eq!(unsafe { libc::pipe(fds.as_mut_ptr()) }, 0, \"pipe()\");\n    remember_extra(fds[1]);\n    (fds[0], fds[1])\n}\"\"\",\n\"\"\"pub fn pipe_pair() -> (i32, i32) {\n    let mut fds = [0i32; 2];\n    assert_eq!(\n        unsafe { libc::pipe2(fds.as_mut_ptr(), libc::O_CLOEXEC) },\n        0,\n        \"pipe2()\"\n    );\n    remember_extra(fds[1]);\n    (fds[0], fds[1])\n}\"\"\")\n\n# 3) run_broken_pipe -> pipe2 O_CLOEXEC\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    let mut fds = [0i32; 2];\n    assert_eq!(unsafe { libc::pipe(fds.as_mut_ptr()) }, 0, \"pipe()\");\n    let (rd, wr) = (fds[0], fds[1]);\"\"\",\n\"\"\"    let mut fds = [0i32; 2];\n    assert_eq!(\n        unsafe { libc::pipe2(fds.as_mut_ptr(), libc::O_CLOEXEC) },\n        0,\n        \"pipe2()\"\n    );\n    let (rd, wr) = (fds[0], fds[1]);\"\"\")\n\n# 4) openpty: mark both ends cloexec\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    assert_eq!(rc, 0, \"openpty failed\");\n    remember_extra(s);\n    (m, s)\"\"\",\n\"\"\"    assert_eq!(rc, 0, \"openpty failed\");\n    set_cloexec(m);\n    set_cloexec(s);\n    remember_extra(s);\n    (m, s)\"\"\")\n\n# 5) from_raw_fd_owned: the dup'd fd must not leak into the child either\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"        let d = libc::dup(fd);\n        assert!(d >= 0, \"dup\");\n        Stdio::from_raw_fd(d)\"\"\",\n\"\"\"        let d = libc::dup(fd);\n        assert!(d >= 0, \"dup\");\n        // dup2 onto fd 0/1 in the child clears FD_CLOEXEC there, so the child\n        // still gets the descriptor - it just does not also inherit this copy.\n        set_cloexec(d);\n        Stdio::from_raw_fd(d)\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"common patched\")\n\np='tests/differential_cli.rs'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    let d = libc::dup(fd);\n    assert!(d >= 0, \"dup\");\n    std::process::Stdio::from_raw_fd(d)\"\"\",\n\"\"\"    let d = libc::dup(fd);\n    assert!(d >= 0, \"dup\");\n    set_cloexec(d);\n    std::process::Stdio::from_raw_fd(d)\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"cli patched\")\nPY\ngrep -c \"set_cloexec\" tests/common/mod.rs tests/differential_cli.rs; grep -c \"pipe2\" tests/common/mod.rs","description":"Set CLOEXEC on all pipe and pty descriptors"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":122714,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":122714,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55ad7133-91d4-4758-8739-8a336070d8f2","uuid":"59fd072f-3af3-43b9-b7ec-bf983454af09","timestamp":"2026-08-17T22:04:37.444Z"}
